{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity"},"metadata":{"title":"Entity","roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Entity","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:11WorldModule6EntityV","modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Entity.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/WorldModule\/Entity.swift#L35"},"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Entity","kind":"identifier"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A handle that identifies one entity in a world."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Entity","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An entity is one thing in your game or simulation. It has no data of its own: a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stores the components it holds, and the handle is how you refer to it. You get a handle by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spawning an entity, and you pass it back to the world to read and change its components:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","let hero = world.spawn(Name(value: \"Ada\"), Health(current: 100))","","print(world[Name.self, of: hero].value)","\/\/ Prints \"Ada\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A handle is a small value, cheap to copy and store, for example in a component that refers to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"another entity. It holds two numbers: the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/index"},{"type":"text","text":" of the slot the entity occupies in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"world, and the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/generation"},{"type":"text","text":" of that slot. When an entity is despawned, the world can reuse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its slot for a new entity with the next generation, so a handle kept past its entity’s despawn"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"stale"}]},{"type":"text","text":": it never names the entity that took the slot."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","let first = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0))","world.despawn(first)","let second = world.spawn(Position(x: 1, y: 1))","","print(first, second)","\/\/ Prints \"0:0 0:1\"","print(world.contains(first))","\/\/ Prints \"false\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Entities are ordered by slot, then by generation."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Operators","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/_(_:_:)"],"title":"Operators","generated":true},{"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/init(from:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/init(index:generation:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/generation","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/index"],"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true},{"anchor":"Defa